        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "This project is a tutorial for libtls (OpenSSL-based TLS library) but includes certificate generation scripts that create classical RSA keys (4096 bits). The RSA keys are used in the certificate authority setup process for generating test certificates. While this is not direct use of crypto APIs in application code, it demonstrates the use of vulnerable classical RSA algorithms in a tutorial context."
